<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Blunt. Ability trait (renamed from UMW_Earthshaker, 2026-07-24 — the TRAIT names the hardware,
       the ABILITY names the act, mirroring Odyssey's EMPPulser trait -> EMPPulse ability) —
       grants AbilityDefs/Earthshake.xml (UMW_Earthshake) via the vanilla
       abilityProps vehicle (WeaponTraitDef.abilityProps : CompProperties_EquippableAbilityReloadable,
       copied onto the weapon's ability comp by CompUniqueWeapon.Setup with zero Harmony; see
       Docs/Specs/Trait-Roster-Expansion.md §5/§2.2 and Earthshake.xml's own header). Pure-cooldown form,
       same shape as Odyssey's EMPPulser trait (just <abilityDef>, no maxCharges/ammo). REQUIRES the
       weapon def to carry CompProperties_EquippableAbilityReloadable in place of plain CompEquippable
       (the §2.2 comps rework, applied to all 7 weapon defs in a parallel change) — CompUniqueWeapon.Setup
       dereferences TryGetComp<CompEquippableAbilityReloadable>() with no null check whenever a rolled
       trait has abilityProps, so a weapon missing the comp would NPE the instant this trait rolls.
       Earthshake's shockwave is indiscriminate (see that def) — say so here too, since a wielder
       choosing/valuing this trait should know their own colonists can be caught in it. The wielder
       themselves is spared (Earthshake's excludeCaster), which is worth stating here as well: it is the
       difference between a trait a player will actually fire and one they will not.
       Tags "Ability" (Odyssey's ability-trait convention) — mutually exclusive with the parallel Melee-
       category trait UMW_Storied's Rallying Cry, so a weapon carries at most one active ability.
       Priced at parity with Odyssey's ranged EMPPulser (+80), c=0.5 per the same ability-trait convention. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_Piledriver</defName>
    <label>piledriver</label>
    <description>The head is built as a piledriver. On command the weapon's full mass can be slammed into the ground, sending a stunning shockwave out through the earth. The shock is indiscriminate; it stuns friend and foe alike, though the braced wielder is spared. Once used, the mechanism takes time to reset.</description>
    <commonality>0.5</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Blunt</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Ability</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <statOffsets>
      <MarketValue>80</MarketValue> <!-- cf. EMPPulser -->
    </statOffsets>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>piledriving</li>
      <li>earthshaking</li>
      <li>quaking</li>
      <li>thunderous</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
    <abilityProps>
      <abilityDef>UMW_Earthshake</abilityDef>
    </abilityProps>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
